{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ba7459a5acae5124", "type": "tool_result", "content": "/tmp/amrd_abs.html\n<head><script>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>  <title>[2607.25289v1] AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition</title>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Abstract page for arXiv paper 2607.25289v1: AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for...\"/>\n  <script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/cite.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script><meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Li, Yuqi\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Lin, Yi-Cheng\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wang, Xianglong\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Yang, Kuo\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Feng, Xiaoqin\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wang, Yixuan\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Duan, Huiran\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Tian, Yingli\" /><meta name=\"citation_date\" content=\"2026/07/28\" /><meta name=\"citation_online_date\" content=\"2026/07/28\" /><meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.25289\" /><meta name=\"citation_arxiv_id\" content=\"2607.25289\" /><meta name=\"citation_abstract\" content=\"On-device speech emotion recognition (SER) is critical for real-time applications, yet large self-supervised models that excel at SER are too costly for edge devices. Multi-teacher knowledge distillation can compress them into a lightweight student, but two challenges remain: teacher reliability varies across batches, and logit-level distillation ignores inter-sample relational structure. We propose Adaptive Multi-teacher Relational Distillation (AMRD) to address both. A one-class SVM on each teacher&#39;s logit similarity matrix assigns per-batch weights favoring more coherent teachers. A relational distillation loss aligns teacher and student similarity matrices, capturing structure that logit matching misses. On IEMOCAP and CREMA-D datasets across four student architectures, AMRD outperforms single-teacher distillation baselines in most settings, and ablations confirm both components yield complementary gains.\" />\n        placeholder=\"Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...\">\n        dc:title=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\"\n    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition</h1>\n    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yuqi Li</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lin,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yi-Cheng Lin</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang,+X\" rel=\"nofollow\">Xianglong Wang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yang,+K\" rel=\"nofollow\">Kuo Yang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Feng,+X\" rel=\"nofollow\">Xiaoqin Feng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yixuan Wang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Duan,+H\" rel=\"nofollow\">Huiran Duan</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Tian,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yingli Tian</a></div>            <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition, by Yuqi Li and 7 other authors</div>\n    <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n            <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>On-device speech emotion recognition (SER) is critical for real-time applications, yet large self-supervised models that excel at SER are too costly for edge devices. Multi-teacher knowledge distillation can compress them into a lightweight student, but two challenges remain: teacher reliability varies across batches, and logit-level distillation ignores inter-sample relational structure. We propose Adaptive Multi-teacher Relational Distillation (AMRD) to address both. A one-class SVM on each teacher&#39;s logit similarity matrix assigns per-batch weights favoring more coherent teachers. A relational distillation loss aligns teacher and student similarity matrices, capturing structure that logit matching misses. On IEMOCAP and CREMA-D datasets across four student architectures, AMRD outperforms single-teacher distillation baselines in most settings, and ablations confirm both components yield complementary gains.\nView a PDF of the paper titled AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition, by Yuqi Li and 7 other authors</div><li><a href=\"/pdf/2607.25289v1\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li><li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.25289v1\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li><li><a href=\"/src/2607.25289v1\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source\n      <div class=\"abs-license\"><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\" class=\"has_license\">\n         accesskey=\"p\" title=\"previous in cs.LG (accesskey p)\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;&nbsp;prev</a>\n         title=\"next in cs.LG (accesskey n)\"  rel=\"nofollow\">next&nbsp;&gt;</a>", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "eca15008-9213-458b-bad6-891a20c53110", "uuid": "e3a04bff-470a-4008-a2d5-e7a07eebff1d", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T09:32:43.202Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "/tmp/amrd_abs.html\n<head><script>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>  <title>[2607.25289v1] AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition</title>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Abstract page for arXiv paper 2607.25289v1: AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for...\"/>\n  <script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/cite.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script><meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Li, Yuqi\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Lin, Yi-Cheng\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wang, Xianglong\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Yang, Kuo\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Feng, Xiaoqin\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wang, Yixuan\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Duan, Huiran\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Tian, Yingli\" /><meta name=\"citation_date\" content=\"2026/07/28\" /><meta name=\"citation_online_date\" content=\"2026/07/28\" /><meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.25289\" /><meta name=\"citation_arxiv_id\" content=\"2607.25289\" /><meta name=\"citation_abstract\" content=\"On-device speech emotion recognition (SER) is critical for real-time applications, yet large self-supervised models that excel at SER are too costly for edge devices. Multi-teacher knowledge distillation can compress them into a lightweight student, but two challenges remain: teacher reliability varies across batches, and logit-level distillation ignores inter-sample relational structure. We propose Adaptive Multi-teacher Relational Distillation (AMRD) to address both. A one-class SVM on each teacher&#39;s logit similarity matrix assigns per-batch weights favoring more coherent teachers. A relational distillation loss aligns teacher and student similarity matrices, capturing structure that logit matching misses. On IEMOCAP and CREMA-D datasets across four student architectures, AMRD outperforms single-teacher distillation baselines in most settings, and ablations confirm both components yield complementary gains.\" />\n        placeholder=\"Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...\">\n        dc:title=\"AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition\"\n    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>AMRD: Adaptive Multi-Teacher Relational Distillation for Lightweight Speech Emotion Recognition</h1>\n    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yuqi Li</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lin,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yi-Cheng Lin</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang,+X\" rel=\"nofollow\">Xianglong Wang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yang,+K\" rel=\"nofollow\">Kuo Yang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Feng,+X\" rel=\"nofollow\">Xiaoqin Feng</a>, <a href=\"https://